@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

### =============================================================================
### Health
### =============================================================================

### Liveness probe — 200 as soon as the process is up
GET {{baseUrl}}/liveness

### Readiness probe — 200 only if every module's database is reachable
GET {{baseUrl}}/readiness


### =============================================================================
### End-to-end happy path
### Run these top to bottom — each request captures an id the next one needs.
### Demonstrates the full saga flow: place order -> approval -> payment -> delivery,
### the last two happening automatically with no further HTTP calls.
### =============================================================================

### 1. Create a restaurant (inactive by default)
# @name createRestaurant
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/restaurants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sakura Sushi",
  "description": "Downtown Japanese restaurant, dine-in and delivery.",
  "amount": 15.00,
  "currency": "Usd",
  "schedules": [
    { "openDay": "Monday", "openTime": "09:00:00", "closeDay": "Monday", "closeTime": "22:00:00" }
  ]
}

### 2. Activate it — otherwise it stays invisible to customers
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/restaurants/{{createRestaurant.response.body.$.id}}/activate

### 3. Add a menu item
# @name addMenuItem
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/restaurants/{{createRestaurant.response.body.$.id}}/menu-items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "California Roll",
  "description": "Crab, avocado, and cucumber, topped with tobiko.",
  "currency": "Usd",
  "amount": 8.50
}

### 4. Create a draft order for that restaurant
# @name createOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/ordering
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "restaurantId": "{{createRestaurant.response.body.$.id}}"
}

### 5. Add the menu item to the order
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/ordering/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/add-items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "menuId": "{{addMenuItem.response.body.$.id}}"
}

### 6. Place the order — kicks off OrderSaga (-> AwaitingApproval), publishes CreateRequest
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/ordering/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/place

### 7. List the restaurant's order requests to find the one the saga just created.
###    This runs async over the message bus — if the array comes back empty, wait a
###    second and re-run this request.
# @name listOrderRequests
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/orderrequests/restaurant/{{createRestaurant.response.body.$.id}}?limit=10

### 8. Approve it — saga proceeds to payment (mock gateway auto-succeeds) and delivery,
###    both created automatically with no further HTTP calls needed.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/orderrequests/{{listOrderRequests.response.body.$[0].orderRequestId}}/approve

### 9. Check the order's final state (should be Confirmed a moment later)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/ordering/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}

### NOTE: Payments/Deliveries are internal saga steps by design — there's no public
### "list payments/deliveries" endpoint, only GetById. To inspect one, grab its id from
### a DB query, log line, or Jaeger trace (http://localhost:16686), then use the
### standalone GET requests in those sections below.


### =============================================================================
### Ordering — standalone requests
### =============================================================================

### Get an order by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/ordering/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}

### Cancel an order — only works before it's placed (fails with Conflict afterward,
### so this needs a fresh draft order — run steps 4-5 again first if you want to try it)
# @name draftOrderToCancel
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/ordering
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "restaurantId": "{{createRestaurant.response.body.$.id}}"
}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/ordering/{{draftOrderToCancel.response.body.$.id}}/cancel


### =============================================================================
### Restaurants — standalone requests
### =============================================================================

@restaurantId = {{createRestaurant.response.body.$.id}}

### Get a restaurant by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}

### Deactivate a restaurant
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/deactivate

### Change name
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/name
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sakura Sushi & Ramen"
}

### Change description
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/description
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Downtown Japanese restaurant, now with ramen."
}

### Replace the opening schedule
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/schedule
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schedules": [
    { "openDay": "Monday", "openTime": "09:00:00", "closeDay": "Monday", "closeTime": "22:00:00" },
    { "openDay": "Saturday", "openTime": "11:00:00", "closeDay": "Sunday", "closeTime": "02:00:00" }
  ]
}

### Set the minimum order price
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/minimal-order-price
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currency": "Usd",
  "amount": 20.00
}

### Remove a menu item
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/menu-items/{{addMenuItem.response.body.$.id}}

### Change a menu item's name
PUT {{baseUrl}}/v1/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/menu-items/{{addMenuItem.response.body.$.id}}/name
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Spicy California Roll"
}

### Change a menu item's description
PUT {{baseUrl}}/v1/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/menu-items/{{addMenuItem.response.body.$.id}}/description
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Crab, avocado, and cucumber, topped with spicy tobiko."
}

### Change a menu item's price
PUT {{baseUrl}}/v1/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/menu-items/{{addMenuItem.response.body.$.id}}/price
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currency": "Usd",
  "amount": 9.50
}


### =============================================================================
### OrderRequests — standalone requests
### =============================================================================

### Get an order request by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/orderrequests/{{listOrderRequests.response.body.$[0].orderRequestId}}

### Reject an order request — run the happy-path flow again first (steps 1-7) to get a
### fresh, still-pending order request; the one from step 8 above is already approved
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/orderrequests/{{listOrderRequests.response.body.$[0].orderRequestId}}/reject


### =============================================================================
### Payments — standalone requests
### No listing endpoint exists (see note above) — replace with a real id
### =============================================================================

### Get a payment by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/payments/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000


### =============================================================================
### Deliveries — standalone requests
### No listing endpoint exists (see note above) — replace with a real id
### =============================================================================

@deliveryId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Get a delivery by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}

### Mark picked up
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/deliveries/pickup/{{deliveryId}}

### Mark completed
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/deliveries/complete/{{deliveryId}}

### Mark failed
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/deliveries/fail/{{deliveryId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Courier could not reach the delivery address."
}
